# stack.branches: source of truth for this fork's PR branches and the combined main.
#
# Two concerns are kept separate on purpose:
#
#   * Each PR branch declares the base it rebases onto, 'base' (upstream, the
#     PR target) or another branch (a real dependency chain). This keeps every
#     branch's PR diff limited to its own work: independent fixes sit on 'base'
#     and never drag each other in.
#
#   * 'assemble' lists the order in which every branch's OWN commits are stacked
#     into the combined 'main' we run. main is a throwaway assembly of
#     cherry-picked copies, never a PR branch.
#
# Keywords:
#   base     <ref>               upstream ref; the PR target and default base.
#   into     <name>              the branch the assembly is written to.
#   branch   <name> onto <ref>   a PR branch; <ref> is 'base' or another branch.
#                                List a parent before any branch that sits on it.
#   assemble <name> ...          build order for the combined branch.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

base upstream/dev
into main

# -- compatibility blockers ---------------------------------------------------
# fix/fast-disk-kwarg removed 2026-09-28: upstream added fast_disk explicitly to
# both patchers (model_patcher.py:361 and :689) and forwards it, so the TypeError
# on every load_unet is gone. Our **kwargs version was only a robustness
# argument, and a weak one - FSDPModelPatcher overrides the load machinery, so
# silently forwarding a parameter it does not honour is worse than a loud
# TypeError. Do not refile.
# fix/xfuser-envs-get-device-name is superseded the same way: upstream now has
# get_device_name() at xfuser_compat.py:124. Out of the build; branch kept until
# it is confirmed unneeded on a render.
branch fix/xfuser-version-bound               onto base

# -- plain bugs, no knobs -----------------------------------------------------
branch fix/dead-actor-recovery                onto base
branch fix/ring-attention-lse-padding         onto base
branch fix/worker-nvrtc-library-path          onto base
branch fix/parallel-quant-shard-load          onto base
branch fix/forward-fast-disk-to-workers       onto base

# -- VRAM lifecycle (a real chain: cancel needs the progress plumbing) --------
# fix/sampler-progress adds _gather_with_progress, which the failure and cancel
# handling builds on. That branch covers a run that goes wrong: VRAM released and
# workers respawned after a failed sample, a cancel that stops the workers with a
# sized wait, and a dead worker failing the job and re-running the initializer.
branch fix/sampler-progress                   onto base
branch fix/worker-failure-and-cancel          onto fix/sampler-progress

# The text encoder reports progress and answers a cancel through the machinery
# fix/sampler-progress adds, so it chains onto it rather than onto base. File
# that one first if these ever go upstream. It also carries its two load fixes:
# moving the encoder off the card while sampling, and loading it on every rank
# before the encode starts.
branch feat/fsdp-text-encoder                 onto fix/sampler-progress
branch fix/offload-quantized-fsdp-shards      onto base
branch fix/free-host-vram-before-shard-load   onto base
branch fix/keep-host-models-when-gpus-pinned  onto base

# -- distributed VAE decode, and cancelling one ------------------------------
# The temporal decode carries its own VRAM fixes: the VAE stays resident where the
# card can spare it, and under clear_vram_after_sampling the workers release it
# after the decode instead of keeping the copy the decode reloaded.
# The temporal decode has no dependency of its own, but the decode's cancel needs
# both its chunk loop and the cancel machinery (progress.request_cancel,
# retire_actors, _drain) from fix/worker-failure-and-cancel, and a branch has one
# base - so the temporal decode sits on the cancel branch to keep the chain linear.
# Cancel and progress for the decode then sit on the temporal decode. The progress bar reports
# through the cancel path's polling wait and counts its chunk loop; it adds
# raylight/decode_progress.py and, like the cancel with progress.py, relies on the
# assembly for a module its own base lacks.
branch feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode         onto fix/worker-failure-and-cancel
branch feat/decode-cancel-and-progress        onto feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode
# feat/decode-pacer and feat/vae-decode-controls are out of the build, like
# tooling/fsdp-probes and tooling/crash-trace. They exist to investigate the
# host-heavy decode phase - the pacer spaces out when each card enters it, the
# controls narrow the fan-out and pin the VAE resident to bisect it. The reserve
# fix removes the phase, so both describe a problem the build no longer has, and
# their node inputs would be four widgets a workflow has no reason to set.

# The Fun ControlNet is a model patch registered on the model itself, so it has to be
# applied inside the workers. Independent of the decode work, so it sits on base. It
# also gives the control patch the full rope table and mod segments: upstream gathers
# img for it but leaves those split, so under USP the two disagree by the world size
# and the feature is wrong without that fix.
branch feat/minimax-h3-fun-controlnet          onto base

# -- features, all off by default --------------------------------------------
# feat/mlp-chunk owns the _mlp_branch extraction so the single pass and the per
# chunk path share one implementation. fp16 narrows that helper on its own
# terms, so the fp16-aware signature is a merge resolution here rather than a
# commit that belongs to neither branch.
branch feat/mlp-chunk                          onto base
# RESOLUTION NOTE: feat/mlp-chunk and feat/minimax-h3-fp16 each add
# `import os as _os` inside the MiniMax injector in usp.py, because each needs it
# on its own. Assembling both leaves the import twice - harmless, Python caches
# the module, but drop one when resolving the fp16 conflict. The two injection
# conditions union to `mlp_chunked or mlp_fp16 or <sidecar>`.
# feat/minimax-h3-fp16 works on stock ComfyUI (load dtype + fp32 text
# preprocessing, both Raylight-side) and defers to ComfyUI's native fp16 block,
# MLP and conditioning where they exist - on our fork that is the path production
# takes. Rendered on upstream ComfyUI and on our fork with the same seed: decoded
# video and audio bit-identical.
branch feat/minimax-h3-fp16                   onto base
branch feat/minimax-h3-fp16-node-inputs       onto feat/minimax-h3-fp16
branch feat/numa-aware-worker-placement       onto base
# Memory for the LoRA bypass: operands kept off the host (opt-in), and the deltas
# added into the layer output in place.
branch feat/lora-bypass-memory                onto base
# ray.shutdown() returns before the old workers have released their GPUs; the
# initializer waits for them before spawning the next set.
branch fix/wait-for-workers-to-exit           onto base
branch feat/rank-gpu-pinning                  onto base
branch fix/ck-patch-scope-nesting             onto base
branch fix/quant-loader-requires-grad        onto base
branch feat/ray-kill-init                    onto base
branch fix/worker-pinned-memory-selectable    onto base
branch feat/worker-vram-tunables-in-workflow  onto base
# Grouping and labels, including clear_vram_after_sampling shown as "Free VRAM"
# and on by default.
branch feat/initializer-input-ux              onto feat/worker-vram-tunables-in-workflow
# Comfy Kitchen INT8 attention as a Raylight inner-attention processor, ring
# support included. Was in the assemble order without a declaration, which
# restack.sh refuses.
branch feat/ck-int8-attention                 onto base

# -- long clips: per-rank memory and failing cleanly --------------------------
# Each rank builds only its slice of the MiniMax H3 sequence and gathers only the
# head's outputs. Touches xdit_context_parallel.py, which the fp16, control-patch
# and ck branches also reshape, so it assembles after all of them.
branch fix/minimax-local-embed-and-head       onto base
# Another RayWorkerOptions knob. Its input is appended last, so it assembles last.
branch feat/collective-timeout-option         onto base

# -- the audio decode -----------------------------------------------------------
# The audio decode on a worker, so its VAE is released under Free VRAM too, with
# its progress bar counted through decode_progress.py - hence onto the video
# progress branch. One worker, deliberately: splitting it across workers measured
# ~-74 dB off bit-identical with no real speed to gain.
branch feat/ray-audio-decode                  onto feat/decode-cancel-and-progress

# -- VRAM and memory fixes found on long clips -------------------------------
# One VAE loader: the distributed decode takes its VAE from RayVAELoader instead of
# loading one by name, and the loader's second output is the same VAE for host
# nodes, loaded there on demand. The decode's chunk loop is
# feat/decode-cancel-and-progress's, so it sits on that branch.
branch feat/single-vae-loader                 onto feat/decode-cancel-and-progress
# Sharding the decoder's weights across the ranks, opt-in per RayVAELoader. It
# replaces the chunk loop's body and adds its option to the loader, so it sits on
# the single-loader branch.
branch feat/fsdp-vae-decode                   onto feat/single-vae-loader
# Workers never ran ComfyUI's reset_cast_buffers, so a streamed VAE stayed pinned
# after the worker dropped it.
branch fix/worker-reset-cast-buffers          onto base
# Moves the DiT off the cards while the text encoder runs; needs the per-rank
# encoder preparation the text encoder branch carries.
branch fix/offload-dit-while-encoding         onto feat/fsdp-text-encoder
# FSDPModelPatcher.load(full_load=True) moved CPU-offloaded shards onto the card.
branch fix/fsdp-full-load-keeps-cpu-offload   onto base
# tooling/crash-trace is NOT declared as a PR branch and is NOT in the build. Its
# markers sit in code owned by two different feature branches (encode_tokens from
# feat/fsdp-text-encoder, the decode path from feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode), so it
# has no single base to rebase onto. It is built on top of an assembled main when a
# crash is being chased and rebuilt from scratch afterwards. An fsync per marker costs
# ~280 us and a shard load is ~1600 of them, so take it back out before quoting timing.

# tooling/fsdp-probes is deliberately NOT in the build: it is measurement
# scaffolding and any timing taken with it armed is unquotable. tooling/crash-trace
# is out for the same reason - it fsyncs a marker per phase, which is what made it
# useful against a host that resets without logging anything and useless for
# timing. trial/crash-trace holds the 2026-09-29 diagnostic state.
#
# tooling/stack IS in the build, and has to be: PHASE 2 checks out the base and
# cherry-picks, so unless the tooling is assembled too, the working tree loses
# restack.sh partway through and cannot be re-run after a conflict stop. It
# carries no code the node imports. It assembles FIRST so that after a conflict
# stop the working tree still has restack.sh to re-run - assembled last, the
# scripts only appear once the build already finished.
branch tooling/stack                          onto base

# Combined main = these branches' own commits, stacked in this order.
# ORDER MATTERS for node inputs: ComfyUI node inputs are POSITIONAL, and saved
# workflows store values by position. feat/rank-gpu-pinning inserts
# pin_ranks_to_gpus at index 4; feat/initializer-input-ux regroups the tail.
# Assembling rank-pinning BEFORE initializer-input-ux reproduces the input order
# the saved workflows in ComfyUI/user/default/workflows were built against.
# verify-restack.sh checks that order explicitly - do not reorder these two
# without re-running it.
assemble tooling/stack fix/xfuser-version-bound fix/dead-actor-recovery fix/ring-attention-lse-padding fix/worker-nvrtc-library-path fix/parallel-quant-shard-load fix/forward-fast-disk-to-workers fix/sampler-progress fix/worker-failure-and-cancel fix/offload-quantized-fsdp-shards fix/free-host-vram-before-shard-load fix/keep-host-models-when-gpus-pinned feat/vae-temporal-chunk-decode feat/decode-cancel-and-progress feat/mlp-chunk feat/minimax-h3-fp16 feat/minimax-h3-fp16-node-inputs feat/numa-aware-worker-placement feat/lora-bypass-memory fix/wait-for-workers-to-exit feat/rank-gpu-pinning feat/ray-kill-init fix/worker-pinned-memory-selectable feat/worker-vram-tunables-in-workflow feat/initializer-input-ux fix/ck-patch-scope-nesting feat/fsdp-text-encoder fix/quant-loader-requires-grad feat/minimax-h3-fun-controlnet feat/ck-int8-attention fix/minimax-local-embed-and-head feat/collective-timeout-option feat/ray-audio-decode feat/single-vae-loader feat/fsdp-vae-decode fix/worker-reset-cast-buffers fix/offload-dit-while-encoding fix/fsdp-full-load-keeps-cpu-offload
